-- Patterning 3 (Olympia Noise Co.) — Mac Catalyst drum machine on this Mac.
-- Exposes a virtual MIDI destination literally called "Patterning 3" when
-- running. Standalone and AUv3 versions both ship.
--
-- Mapping origin: authored directly into
--   ~/Library/Group Containers/group.olympianoiseco.patterning/ApplicationSupport/MIDI Input Mappings/PurerlTidal.patterningMIDIMapping
-- Format is NSKeyedArchiver binary plist. Each entry has fields:
-- {midiStatus, midiChannel, midiData, midiSource, key, track, min, max,
--  exponent, storedIndex, displayString}. The `midiSource` field is exact
-- match by upstream port name — we author with "Patterning 3" so messages
-- arriving on Patterning's own input port match.
--
-- Architecture: channel-per-track for CCs (track N → channel N, 1..8) so
-- each track follows GM convention on its own channel. Triggers stay on
-- channel 1 with note numbers 60–72 (the factory defaults: C major scale
-- C4..C5). Master controls on channel 16.
--
-- After `load patterning3`, bindings become pattern lanes:
--   p3-1                 "x ~ x x ~ x x ~"   -- triggers Track 1
--   p3-1-volume          "0.8 0.7 0.5 0.7"   -- per-step gain on Track 1
--   p3-3-cutoff          (slow 4 sine)       -- Track 3 filter sweep
--
-- Triggering: send notes to channel 1 on Patterning 3 (notes 60–72 → tracks
-- 1–8). Per-track shaping via CCs on channel N. The per-track CC layout is
-- intentionally GM-like so that hand controllers (Twister etc.) map without
-- relearning.
--
-- Hand-controller FX surface lives in a SEPARATE mapping file (planned —
-- not authored here) — distortion / EQ / compressor parameters target
-- continuous tactile manipulation, not sequenced patterns.
--
-- Choke groups are exposed (CC 16 per channel) so purerl-tidal can sequence
-- track-cuts-track relationships rhythmically.

-- lat 0: calibrated against Patterning's internal sequencer with
-- the OSC→link-spike→CoreMIDI dispatch path (cross-correlation peak
-- lag 0.25 ms, std jitter 4.4 ms — the residual jitter is Patterning's
-- audio buffer, not the dispatch). The previous 30 ms placeholder was
-- there to compensate for `os:cmd sendmidi` subprocess overhead; with
-- the new dispatch path no compensation is needed.
midi-device patterning "Patterning 3" lat 0

-- ─── Track triggers (factory defaults — notes on channel 1) ───────────
-- Each `bind p3-N` triggers track N. Pattern tokens fire the trigger note;
-- ~ silences. 200ms duration matches Laplace defaults (long enough for the
-- sample to start cleanly, short enough to avoid overlap at common BPMs).
bind p3-1                  midi-note patterning 1 60 100 200
bind p3-2                  midi-note patterning 1 62 100 200
bind p3-3                  midi-note patterning 1 64 100 200
bind p3-4                  midi-note patterning 1 65 100 200
bind p3-5                  midi-note patterning 1 67 100 200
bind p3-6                  midi-note patterning 1 69 100 200
bind p3-7                  midi-note patterning 1 71 100 200
bind p3-8                  midi-note patterning 1 72 100 200

-- ─── Track 1 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bind p3-1-volume           midi-cc patterning 1 7
bind p3-1-pan              midi-cc patterning 1 10
bind p3-1-coarse           midi-cc patterning 1 14
bind p3-1-fine             midi-cc patterning 1 15
bind p3-1-choke            midi-cc patterning 1 16
bind p3-1-resonance        midi-cc patterning 1 71
bind p3-1-attack           midi-cc patterning 1 73
bind p3-1-cutoff           midi-cc patterning 1 74
bind p3-1-decay            midi-cc patterning 1 75
bind p3-1-reverb           midi-cc patterning 1 91
bind p3-1-delay            midi-cc patterning 1 93

-- ─── Track 2 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bind p3-2-volume           midi-cc patterning 2 7
bind p3-2-pan              midi-cc patterning 2 10
bind p3-2-coarse           midi-cc patterning 2 14
bind p3-2-fine             midi-cc patterning 2 15
bind p3-2-choke            midi-cc patterning 2 16
bind p3-2-resonance        midi-cc patterning 2 71
bind p3-2-attack           midi-cc patterning 2 73
bind p3-2-cutoff           midi-cc patterning 2 74
bind p3-2-decay            midi-cc patterning 2 75
